  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "report_markdown": "## Executive Summary\n\n- The `.x` function is the only way to perform output in Unlambda.\n- The `.x` function prints the character x on the standard output.\n- `r` is a shorthand for `.` and prints a newline, returning its argument.\n- `e` is the Exit function that halts evaluation.\n- The backquote (ASCII number 96=0x60) represents Unlambda's apply operation.\n- The r function prints a newline and .* prints an asterisk in Unlambda.\n- In Unlambda, the ` character is used to apply a function to its argument.\n- In Unlambda, `.x outputs the character x.\n",
